      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "What does it mean to listen when the earth itself is speaking?\n\nNigamon/Tunai is a powerful poetic manifesto by Émilie Monnet (Anishinaabe/French) and Waira Nina (Inga Nation, Colombian Amazon). This immersive performance invites you to sit on stage with the artists, surrounded by living trees, pools of water, and copper instruments that sing with flowing water.\n\nAt the heart of the work is a confrontation with the destruction of water and land in the Colombian Amazon caused by Canadian mining companies extracting copper—a..."
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns/fb#admins": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "728780803"
      }
    ],
